 "summary": "Both support theorems are new: no hypergeometric support result exists in TauCeti or Mathlib, and the proofs reuse the existing mass criterion, `Measure.support_map_eq_closure_image`, and the closedness of finite sets. The inline argument that support on a discrete space equals the points with nonzero mass matches a pattern already written out by hand in main, and no shared lemma exists to replace it, so it is not a blocking duplication.",
